re":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_07f5ee05931c6d410169c417f6bc808191a52219d0605eda18\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Bd0Ucsv6C5wadLHDZzAqlS2L|fc_07f5ee05931c6d410169c417f76da8819183a5e3a5bd582a56","name":"sessions_spawn","arguments":{"runtime":"subagent","mode":"run","label":"loopai-doctor-agent-synthetic-distillation-test","task":"You are acting as the LoopAI Doctor Agent for a synthetic workflow test only. Do not treat any of the following as real patient data. Your job is to perform an LLM distillation-style patient-facing summary from the provided synthetic conversation context and synthetic diagnostic tool output.\n\nRequirements:\n- Explicitly state this is a synthetic test case, not a real diagnosis.\n- Keep clinical uncertainty visible.\n- Distinguish between user-reported symptoms and tool-derived findings.\n- Produce a concise patient-facing report with clear sections.\n- End with suggested next steps and a note that the output is a preliminary interpretation only.\n\nSynthetic conversation context:\n- Adult user reports 3 days of right flank discomfort, mild nausea, and intermittent fatigue.\n- No fever reported.\n- No vomiting reported.\n- Urination described as slightly more frequent than usual.\n- Pain is described as dull, 4/10, not clearly positional.\n- User is worried because of a past history of kidney stones.\n\nSynthetic diagnostic tool output:\n1) Urinalysis prototype output:\n- Trace blood detected\n- Leukocyte esterase: negative\n- Nitrites: negative\n- Protein: negative\n- Specific gravity: mildly elevated\n\n2) Basic lab prototype output:\n- Creatinine: within normal range\n- eGFR: within normal range\n- WBC count: within normal range\n- CRP: not elevated\n\n3) Renal ultrasound prototype summary:\n- Mild right-sided hydronephrosis\n- Possible small proximal ureteral stone not directly visualized\n- No renal mass seen\n\nPlease return only the distilled patient-facing report."},"partialJson":"{\"runtime\":\"subagent\",\"